{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "534205cd-61cf-4f16-95b5-4966f792cba3",
    "name": "Cleanora R1-P00 Foundation",
    "description": "# Cleanora R1-P00 — Foundation\n\n> **API version:** `/api/v1`  \n> **Collection environments:** `Hosted (Not hosted yet)` and `Local`\n\nR1-P00 establishes the first externally observable Cleanora system-health\ncontract. This collection is intentionally small: it verifies that the HTTP\nprocess is alive and that required application dependencies are ready.\n\n## Collection Structure\n\n```text\nHosted (Not hosted yet)\n└── System\n    ├── Liveness\n    └── Readiness\n\nLocal\n└── System\n    ├── Liveness\n    └── Readiness\n```\n\nHosted requests use `{{hostUrl}}`; Local requests use `{{baseUrl}}`.\n\n## Requests\n\n### Liveness\n\n```http\nGET {{baseUrl}}/system/health/live\n```\n\nConfirms that the API process can receive and answer HTTP requests. It does not\nprove that PostgreSQL or every required dependency is available.\n\n### Readiness\n\n```http\nGET {{baseUrl}}/system/health/ready\n```\n\nConfirms that the application is ready to serve dependency-backed traffic. A\ndependency failure may produce `503 Service Unavailable` with a safe error\nenvelope.\n\n## Saved Examples\n\nEvery request contains a Saved Example named `Success`. Expand the request in\nPostman to inspect the request URL, HTTP status, and representative Cleanora\nresponse envelope.\n\n## Standard Success Envelope\n\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"status\": \"ok\"\n  },\n  \"requestId\": \"request_example_01\"\n}\n```\n\n## Running Locally\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n```text\nLocal API: http://localhost:8000/api/v1\nSwagger:   http://localhost:8000/api/v1/docs\n```\n\nThe health requests require no Bearer token and have no request body.\n\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Hosted (Not hosted yet)",
      "description": "Health requests using {{hostUrl}}. Configure/select the hosted environment before use.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "System",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "Liveness",
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "const body = pm.response.json();",
                      "pm.test(\"Expected health status\", () => pm.expect([200]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                      "pm.test('Uses a correlated Cleanora response envelope', () => {",
                      "  pm.expect(body.requestId).to.be.a('string');",
                      "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-request-id')).to.eql(body.requestId);",
                      "  if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                      "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                      "    pm.expect(body.data.status).to.eql('ok');",
                      "  }",
                      "});"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ],
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Accept",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "url": "{{hostUrl}}/system/health/live",
                "description": "Returns 200 when the liveness health contract succeeds.",
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "response": [
                {
                  "name": "Success",
                  "originalRequest": {
                    "method": "GET",
                    "header": [
                      {
                        "key": "Accept",
                        "value": "application/json"
                      }
                    ],
                    "url": "{{hostUrl}}/system/health/live",
                    "description": "Returns 200 when the liveness health contract succeeds.",
                    "auth": {
                      "type": "noauth"
                    }
                  },
                  "status": "OK",
                  "code": 200,
                  "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
                  "header": [
                    {
                      "key": "Content-Type",
                      "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "x-request-id",
                      "value": "request_example_01"
                    }
                  ],
                  "cookie": [],
                  "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"status\": \"ok\"\n  },\n  \"requestId\": \"request_example_01\"\n}"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Readiness",
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "const body = pm.response.json();",
                      "pm.test(\"Expected health status\", () => pm.expect([200, 503]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                      "pm.test('Uses a correlated Cleanora response envelope', () => {",
                      "  pm.expect(body.requestId).to.be.a('string');",
                      "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-request-id')).to.eql(body.requestId);",
                      "  if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                      "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                      "    pm.expect(body.data.status).to.eql('ready');",
                      "  }",
                      "});",
                      "if (pm.response.code === 503) {",
                      "  pm.test('Returns a safe dependency failure', () => {",
                      "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(false);",
                      "    pm.expect(body.error).to.include({ code: 'DEPENDENCY_NOT_READY', statusCode: 503 });",
                      "    pm.expect(JSON.stringify(body)).not.to.match(/postgres(?:ql)?:\\/\\/|DATABASE_URL|SELECT\\s/i);",
                      "  });",
                      "}"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ],
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Accept",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "url": "{{hostUrl}}/system/health/ready",
                "description": "Returns 200 when healthy or 503 DEPENDENCY_NOT_READY without leaking infrastructure details.",
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "response": [
                {
                  "name": "Success",
                  "originalRequest": {
                    "method": "GET",
                    "header": [
                      {
                        "key": "Accept",
                        "value": "application/json"
                      }
                    ],
                    "url": "{{hostUrl}}/system/health/ready",
                    "description": "Returns 200 when healthy or 503 DEPENDENCY_NOT_READY without leaking infrastructure details.",
                    "auth": {
                      "type": "noauth"
                    }
                  },
                  "status": "OK",
                  "code": 200,
                  "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
                  "header": [
                    {
                      "key": "Content-Type",
                      "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "x-request-id",
                      "value": "request_example_01"
                    }
                  ],
                  "cookie": [],
                  "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"status\": \"ready\"\n  },\n  \"requestId\": \"request_example_01\"\n}"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
